(8940, 497, 'featured_image_2', '221'),
(8941, 497, '_featured_image_2', 'field_644be71e78ecb'),
(8942, 497, 'youtube_video', ''),
(8943, 497, '_youtube_video', 'field_644be72f78ecc'),
(8944, 497, 'section_2_title', 'Our Instructors'),
(8945, 497, '_section_2_title', 'field_644be7c178ed3'),
(8946, 497, 'section_2_title_copy', 'At Color of Hope, we have had the opportunity to organize multiple one-day workshops with various instructors, but we are fortunate to have three dedicated teachers who take regular classes for our children. Sneha and Namita, two compassionate undergraduate students, conduct classes for three girls who are preparing for their board exams, even though they have to do so on the footpath due to lack of shelter. Meanwhile, Sumana Ma\'am, our music instructor, takes weekly classes and is passionate about teaching our children. We are grateful for their commitment and contribution to the education and growth of our children.'),
(8947, 497, '_section_2_title_copy', 'field_644be7d578ed4'),
(8948, 497, 'section_2_content', '3'),
(8949, 497, '_section_2_content', 'field_644be74878ece'),
(8950, 497, 'newsletter_title', 'Brighter Horizons - A Newsletter Of Ramdhanu Society'),
(8951, 497, '_newsletter_title', 'field_644be817597e2'),
(8952, 497, 'newsletter_subtitle', 'Bringing You The Latest Updates On Our Efforts To Build A Better Future For All Children'),
(8953, 497, '_newsletter_subtitle', 'field_644be834597e3'),
(8954, 497, 'section_4_contents', '2'),
(8955, 497, '_section_4_contents', 'field_644be85327417'),
(8956, 497, 'section_4_contents_0_section4_image', '446'),
(8957, 497, '_section_4_contents_0_section4_image', 'field_644be8882741a'),
(8958, 497, 'section_4_contents_0_alignment', 'right'),
(8959, 497, '_section_4_contents_0_alignment', 'field_644be8972741b'),
(8960, 497, 'section_4_contents_0_section4_title', '<h3>Special Children at Ramdhanu\'s Colour of Hope Project: Embracing Inclusivity and Equality</h3>\r\nAt Ramdhanu Social Welfare Society, we believe in practicing what we preach. Our commitment to inclusiveness and equality is reflected in our support of children like Paridhi and Prabhas, who both face unique challenges.\r\n\r\nParidhi, who has Down syndrome, was unfortunately rejected by mainstream schools despite her mother\'s efforts to enroll her. However, she has found a welcoming and supportive community in Ramdhanu. Paridhi actively participates in all of our projects, classes, and workshops, showcasing her intelligence and lovable nature.\r\n\r\nMeanwhile, we have been caring for Prabhas since the beginning of our journey. Prabhas is a street child who is autistic and unable to communicate, talk, or walk. We provide him with medical assistance and nutritious food, ensuring that he receives the care and support he needs. Prabhas\'s mother, Sonali, who works as a house help, is also involved in our \"Wellbeing Of Women\" project.\r\n\r\nAt Ramdhanu, we firmly believe that all children deserve love, care, and the opportunity to thrive. Through our Color Of Hope project, we are committed to creating a safe and inclusive environment for all children, regardless of their abilities.'),
(8961, 497, '_section_4_contents_0_section4_title', 'field_644be8cf2741d'),
(8962, 497, 'section_4_contents_1_section4_image', '449'),
(8963, 497, '_section_4_contents_1_section4_image', 'field_644be8882741a'),
(8964, 497, 'section_4_contents_1_alignment', 'left'),
(8965, 497, '_section_4_contents_1_alignment', 'field_644be8972741b'),
(8966, 497, 'section_4_contents_1_section4_title', '<h3>Chuti Didir Pathshala: Empowering Young Minds</h3>\r\nAt Ramdhanu, we believe that every child deserves access to education, regardless of their background or socioeconomic status. That\'s why we\'re proud to have our youngest member, Abherii, leading the way with her special project, Chuti Didir Pathshala.\r\n\r\nChuti, also known as Abherii, has been actively involved in our projects and recently started teaching street children during the pandemic. Her passion for education and empowering young minds led her to start Chuti Didir Pathshala, where she provides education and care to small children who cannot afford preschool.\r\n\r\nWe believe that every child deserves a chance to learn and grow, and Chuti Didir Pathshala is just one way we\'re working to make that a reality. Through this project, we hope to inspire and empower young minds to reach their full potential and pave the way for a brighter future.'),
(8967, 497, '_section_4_contents_1_section4_title', 'field_644be8cf2741d'),
